# Anchored to the repo root on purpose. wrangler.toml's build step generates
# ./public from an allowlist, so that one directory must stay untracked -- but
# an UNANCHORED `public/` matches any directory of that name at any depth, and
# it was silently swallowing racing-v2/public/ (the game's source audio). A
# fresh clone would have been unable to build the game, with no error to
# explain why, because git does not report what it is ignoring.
/public/
node_modules/
.wrangler/
.ai-reviews/
logs/*.tmp
scripts/.cache/
scripts/__pycache__/
logs/
.claude/
.DS_Store
temporal/node_modules/
temporal/temporal-dev.db
temporal/temporal-dev.db-shm
temporal/temporal-dev.db-wal
temporal/logs/
.refs/
